{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B8iy2Yeeyr12zZEAu",
	"notes": "A full Astropath of the Adeptus Astra Telepathica: Beta-grade (Psyker Talent 3), soul-bound to the Emperor's light and blinded in the binding ritual, trained in Telepathy as their core discipline (which includes Astrotelepathy, their signature interstellar-relay power). Point math: 90 (attributes) + 10 (Unusual Background) + 30 (Psyker 3) - 15 (Sanctioned Psyker) - 55 (Soulbinding) + 9 (Witch-sight) + ~140 (Telepathy discipline at default starting levels, dominated by Mind Probe/Dominate's alternative-abilities cost) + skills. The Blindness and Soulbinding costs pull the raw total down hard, which is intentional — an Astropath trades an enormous amount for their gift, offset here by strong mental attributes and a powerful, wide-ranging Telepathy list; total should land in framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier once skills and personal equipment are added. GCS will compute the exact final total from the included traits' own modifiers; treat the figures above as this template's design-time estimate, not a promise of GCS's rounding.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tYBwhRfgxDD6WqUYM",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Astropath's body is unremarkable; their mind and soul are what the Choir selects for.\n\nDesign: ST 10 (human baseline), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tT9Bl3OywdfolkmD3",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Astropaths are not soldiers, and rarely fight.\n\nDesign: DX 10 (human baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "t_ch0Tr3teggEo-CD",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Choir draws its strongest telepaths from unusually sharp, focused minds.\n\nDesign: IQ 12 (+2 from baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40
		},
		{
			"id": "tRQT3Qe6_Dq4Kvd-D",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Average endurance; the ritual that makes an Astropath costs the eyes, not the body's toughness.\n\nDesign: HT 10 (human baseline), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tYUYviOWUFkmeFHbt",
			"name": "Will",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Astropath's entire function depends on an exceptionally strong will — to hold an interstellar link open, and to survive doing so.\n\nDesign: Will+4 (Basic's Increased Will, 5 pts/level, B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 4,
			"base_points": 20
		},
		{
			"id": "tz5WyYQ3E-Omq1tG9",
			"name": "Unusual Background (Latent Psychic Potential)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Psychic ability is a random, rare mutation of the human genome that lets its bearer perceive and touch the immaterium (the warp). Sources disagree on exact frequency — Imperial administrative texts and Dark Heresy-line background both describe it as \"rare but not vanishingly so,\" on the order of a handful of latent potentials per hive-sized population, with usably strong psykers far rarer still. Treat any precise ratio as flavour, not census data.\n\nDesign: Required to take Psyker (Talent) or any trait carrying the Warp power modifier below. Basic Set B261 leaves Unusual Background costs to the GM; 10 points reflects that the ability itself is not learned but grants access to an entire framework of further abilities, roughly the going rate other published settings use for \"you may buy from this power list at all.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "t8D63UDgmBAg69h2x",
			"name": "Psyker",
			"reference": "B89",
			"local_notes": "Applies to: Meditation, Hidden Lore (the Warp), and the Will roll to\nresist Perils of the Warp (see above) — a house extension of Talent's\nnormal \"add to listed skills\" rule, precedented by Magery's own habit of\naiding related rolls beyond pure spellcasting. Reaction bonus: +1/level\nfrom other sanctioned psykers and the Astra Telepathica.\n\nImperial Assignment scale (Adeptus Astra Telepathica / Black Ships),\nweakest to strongest, mapped to Talent level and the practical ceiling on\nany single ability's level/dice bought with it:\n  Iota    — Talent 0 (latent; register but rarely take Psyker traits at all)\n  Zeta    — Talent 1, ability cap ~2\n  Eta     — Talent 1, ability cap ~2\n  Theta   — Talent 2, ability cap ~3\n  Epsilon — Talent 2, ability cap ~4  (typical Wyrdvane conscript)\n  Delta   — Talent 3, ability cap ~5  (typical Sanctioned Primaris Psyker)\n  Gamma   — Talent 4, ability cap ~6\n  Beta    — Talent 4, ability cap ~7  (many Astropaths)\n  Alpha   — Talent 5, ability cap ~8  (Astartes Librarians, Black Ship candidates)\n  Alpha-Plus — Talent 6+, ability cap 9+ (beyond-play tier: Primarchs,\n    the most powerful Inquisitors, the worst Chaos sorcerers)\n\nLore: The Iota-to-Alpha-Plus assignment scale is drawn from the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's own grading of psychic potential as depicted across Dark Heresy-line material and repeated in Codex/Imperial Armour background; Black Library uses the same grades in passing (e.g. Eisenhorn-cycle and Ciaphas Cain references to Alpha-class talents). \"Alpha-Plus\" specifically denotes the rarest, most dangerous talents the Black Ships process.\n\nDesign: Talent affecting three things (two skills plus the Perils resistance roll) sits at Basic's \"Medium Talent\" rate of 10 points/level (B90, three-to-five-skill bracket) rather than 5 (one-two skills) or 15 (six-nine skills). Capped at level 6 for player characters; higher grades are GM-reference only, per the framework's \"Beyond play\" tier.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 3,
			"base_points": 0,
			"max_levels": 6
		},
		{
			"id": "TxNqK_9kK3UXzCXLs",
			"name": "Sanctioned Psyker",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Sanctioned psyker has passed through the Scholastia Psykana or an equivalent rite, is legally registered, and typically serves the Astra Militarum, an Inquisitor, or their Chapter's Librarius. They are watched, bound by oath and duty, and — even legally protected — are still called \"witch\" behind their back by the citizens they defend. Consistent across Dark Heresy/Only War's Sanctioned-psyker rules and Black Library's depiction of Primaris Psykers and Astartes Librarians alike.\n\nDesign: Duty to the Astra Telepathica/Inquisition (Basic B133 Duty table, hazardous, 12 or less) at -10, plus a mild, legally-protected Social Stigma (\"sanctioned witch,\" -5, lighter than Basic's Minority Group tier because the law is nominally on their side). Net -15.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Social",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tsrs-wBtELNa6DTdI",
					"name": "Duty (Astra Telepathica/Inquisition, 12 or less)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See parent trait.\n\nDesign: See parent trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -10
				},
				{
					"id": "tC-YXZiSefGSfrPjo",
					"name": "Social Stigma (Sanctioned Psyker)",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See parent trait.\n\nDesign: See parent trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Social",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TuROSuSrssR4vmMH8",
			"name": "Soulbinding (Astropathic Choir)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: To become an Astropath, a Sanctioned psyker undergoes the soul-binding ritual: their eyes are burned out and their mind is bound, in a small part, to the Emperor's own psychic light on the Astronomican, so that their thoughts can be found and carried across interstellar distances. They are permanently blind and permanently, irrevocably in the Emperor's and the Imperium's service from that day on. This is standard background across Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's Astropath material and referenced throughout Black Library whenever an Astropathic Choir appears (e.g. the Horus Heresy's Astropaths aboard Legion flagships).\n\nDesign: Blindness (Basic B140, -50) is the dominant cost; it is not mitigated mechanically here (their remaining \"sight\" is represented by Witch-sight and their Telepathy powers, not a vision substitute). Mindlink to the Astronomican/the Emperor's light (Basic Mindlink, a specific \"person,\" 5 points) is a genuine benefit — it is how they are found and relayed across the void. Sense of Duty to the Imperium of Man (a very-large-group Sense of Duty, -10, Basic's tier below \"entire race\") completes the package. Net -55.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tNEt3Qh_3fz_ABX8i",
					"name": "Blindness",
					"reference": "B140",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See parent trait.\n\nDesign: See parent trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -50
				},
