					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "t1EZYv80lJTij-bSY",
					"name": "Astrotelepathy",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The astropath's signature act: sending and receiving thought across interstellar distances, relayed choir to choir and, ultimately, through the Astronomican itself. Astropaths who fail badly during a transmission are a recurring Black Library beat (burned out, driven mad, or lost with the ship's Geller field).\n\nDesign: Base 20 points for a mental send-and-receive package is this project's own baseline (Basic's exact per-range-step Telecommunication costs are not confidently recalled, so this figure is fixed for internal consistency rather than cited to a page); Increased Range at the highest tabled step (+60%) for interstellar reach, Preparation Required (-20%, a ritual trance), and the Severe Perils tier for the real danger of transmitting through the warp.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m8aVVWSwbBGsH2Frm",
							"name": "Increased Range x100",
							"cost_adj": "+60%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mVHNnC1S4NLhZWsPf",
							"name": "Preparation Required",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mpwUmUTTgUY6lAsUU",
							"name": "Warp",
							"cost_adj": "-15%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m3MUB4FAnCfE0a_KV",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 20
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sDkxqdiqVX6wBolww",
			"name": "Psyniscience",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trained (or instinctive) sense of \"something wrong\" in a presence, place, or object touched by the warp — a chill in a corridor, a servitor's dead eyes going wrong. Named for the Dark Heresy/Only War skill of the same purpose (Psyniscience), used here for calibration only; the GURPS build is original.\n\nDesign: New skill per framework.md (\"New skills only when nothing fits\"). Per/H, Talent-affected: characters with a Psyker Talent (see the psyker power library — not part of this file) get it at a discount per that trait's rules and may default it from Per at a penalty; an unaugmented human without any psychic Talent cannot default into it at all (there is nothing latent to sense with) and must buy it as an unusual background purchase, if a GM allows it at all — most unaugmented Imperial citizens simply never take this skill.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Psionic"
			],
			"difficulty": "per/h",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "snIL3SWTTHG-j-P3u",
			"name": "Meditation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trance discipline an Astropath uses to hold an interstellar link open for hours.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (12) for 4 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sciAU6rRZO-wXEJia",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Deep doctrinal knowledge of the immaterium, taught to every soul-bound Astropath.\n\nDesign: IQ+1 (13) for 4 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"specialization": "the Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sAvcp4UC5jWlxhicS",
			"name": "Theology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Astropath's faith in the Emperor is, quite literally, load-bearing.\n\nDesign: IQ-1 (11) for 2 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"specialization": "Imperial Creed",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
